  "question": {
    "text": "For any vectora a the value of $(\\vec{a} \\times \\hat{i})^2+(\\vec{a} \\times \\hat{j})^2+(\\vec{a} \\times \\hat{k})^2$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xITyr",
      "text": "\n$3 \\vec{a}^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "epV1U",
      "text": "\n$\\vec{a}^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wXwlX",
      "text": "\n$2 \\vec{a}^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "DovxR",
      "text": "\n$4 \\vec{a}^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $\\vec{a}=x \\hat{i}+y \\hat{j}+z \\hat{k}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\vec{a} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{i}}=z \\hat{\\mathbf{j}}-y \\hat{\\mathbf{k}} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow(\\vec{a} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{i}})^2=y^2+z^2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nsimilarly $(\\vec{a} \\times \\hat{j})^2=x^2+z^2$\nand $(\\vec{a} \\times \\hat{k})^2=x^2+y^2 \\Rightarrow(\\vec{a} \\times \\hat{i})^2=y^2+z^2$\nsimilarly $(\\vec{a} \\times \\hat{j})^2=x^2+z^2$\nand $(\\vec{a} \\times \\hat{k})^2=x^2+y^2$\n$$\n\\Rightarrow(\\vec{a} \\times \\hat{i})^2+(\\vec{a} \\times \\hat{j})^2+(\\vec{a} \\times \\hat{k})^2=2\\left(x^2+y^2+z^2\\right)=2 \\vec{a}^2 .\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
